    <summary>Universal Machine Learning Runtime for Windows with DirectML GPU acceleration</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
# CoreMLWin - Universal ML Runtime

High-performance machine learning runtime for Windows that brings Apple CoreML-like experience with DirectML GPU acceleration.

## Features

- ✅ **ONNX Runtime Integration** - Run any ONNX model
- ✅ **DirectML GPU Acceleration** - Harness Windows GPU power (NVIDIA, AMD, Intel)
- ✅ **CPU Fallback** - Automatic fallback when GPU unavailable
- ✅ **Python SDK** - Easy-to-use Python client library
- ✅ **C++ API** - Native performance for C++ applications
- ✅ **Production Ready** - Comprehensive error handling and logging
- ✅ **Secure** - Red-team tested with defense in depth

## Requirements

- Windows 10 version 1903 (build 18362) or newer
- DirectX 12 capable GPU (for GPU acceleration)
- Latest GPU drivers

## Quick Start

After installation:

```powershell
# Start the service
sc start CoreMLWin

# Install Python SDK
pip install coremlwin

# Run inference
python
>>> from coremlwin_client import CoreMLWinClient
>>> client = CoreMLWinClient()
>>> client.health()
{'ready': True, 'version': '0.1.0'}
```

## Package Notes

- Installs to: `C:\ProgramData\chocolatey\lib\coremlwin\tools`
- Includes: ONNX Runtime 1.16.3, DirectML, Python SDK, CLI tools
- Auto-start: Service can be configured to start automatically
- Updates: Use `choco upgrade coremlwin` to update

## Documentation

- Installation Guide: https://github.com/user/WinCoreML/blob/main/docs/INSTALLATION.md
- API Reference: https://github.com/user/WinCoreML/blob/main/docs/API.md
- Testing Guide: https://github.com/user/WinCoreML/blob/main/docs/TESTING.md
]]></description>

